# Super Moist Chocolate Cupcakes

Based on [Sally’s Baking Addiction](https://sallysbakingaddiction.com/super-moist-chocolate-cupcakes/)

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 3/4 cup (94g) [all-purpose flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" } (spooned & leveled)
- [ ] 1/2 cup (41g) [unsweetened natural cocoa powder]{ ing="unsweetened-natural-cocoa-powder" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [espresso powder]{ ing="espresso-powder" } or instant espresso
- [ ] 3/4 tsp [baking powder]{ ing="baking-powder" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [baking soda]{ ing="baking-soda" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 2 large [eggs]{ ing="egg" }, at room temperature
- [ ] 1/2 cup (100g) [granulated sugar]{ ing="granulated-sugar" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup (100g) [packed light brown sugar]{ ing="packed-light-brown-sugar" }
- [ ] 1/3 cup (80ml) [vegetable or canola oil]{ ing="vegetable-or-canola-oil" } (or melted coconut oil)
- [ ] 2 tsp [pure vanilla extract]{ ing="pure-vanilla-extract" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup (120ml) [buttermilk]{ ing="buttermilk" }, at room temperature
- [ ] [Chocolate buttercream and sprinkles]{ ing="chocolate-buttercream-and-sprinkles" } for decorating

## Recipe

1. Preheat oven to 350°F (177°C). Line a 12-count muffin pan with cupcake liners and a second pan with 2 liners (recipe yields about 14 cupcakes).
1. Whisk [flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" }, [cocoa powder]{ ing="unsweetened-natural-cocoa-powder" }, [espresso powder]{ ing="espresso-powder" }, [baking powder]{ ing="baking-powder" }, [baking soda]{ ing="baking-soda" }, and [salt]{ ing="salt" } together. In a medium bowl, whisk [eggs]{ ing="egg" }, [sugars]{ ing="granulated-sugar" }, [oil]{ ing="vegetable-or-canola-oil" }, and vanilla until smooth. Combine wet and dry ingredients alternately with [buttermilk]{ ing="buttermilk" }, stirring gently until just combined—do not overmix.
1. Fill liners only halfway (critical to prevent overflow). Bake 18-21 minutes until a toothpick inserted in the center comes out clean. Cool completely before frosting.
1. Frost with chocolate buttercream.

## Notes

- Store covered in the refrigerator up to 3 days.
